     <h2 style="margin:0.6rem 0 1rem">Most quality systems do not fail for lack of knowledge. They fail for lack of calendar.</h2>
     <p style="color:var(--text-muted);max-width:78ch">The supplier reevaluation nobody remembered, the internal audit squeezed into the last week before the visit, the management review held in a hurry with half the inputs missing: these are the findings auditors raise most often, and they are all scheduling failures. Prompt 9 builds your annual QMS activity calendar from the frequencies in your procedures, a twelve month plan with owners and expected outputs, every date marked as proposed so you adjust it as reality moves. Your system stops living in someone's memory and starts living on a schedule.</p>
